# Daily ownership sync -- install with:  crontab -e
#
# Runs the pipeline only. It never writes to the CRM; it refreshes the website
# and CRM snapshots, regenerates proposals, and leaves them in the review queue.
# A human still approves each change in the review app.
#
# 02:00 local, every day. Output is appended to a log; the wrapper keeps the
# last run's exit code so you can alert on failures (exit 2) separately from
# "there is work to review" (exit 1).

BELLHAVEN_TOKEN=bh_your_token_here

0 2 * * * cd /path/to/clipboard && /usr/bin/python3 pipeline.py >> data/sync.log 2>&1; \
          [ $? -eq 2 ] && echo "ownership sync FAILED $(date)" >> data/sync-errors.log

# Then review whenever convenient:
#     cd /path/to/clipboard && python3 app.py --live
#
# Re-running is safe at any frequency. Proposals carry stable fingerprints and
# the decision ledger (data/decisions.db) suppresses anything already approved
# or rejected, so a second run on unchanged data produces an empty queue.
